<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cotentin Peninsula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">Cotentin</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cotentin Peninsula is a peninsula of Normandy in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, projecting into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>, with the port of Cherbourg at its tip. In Gaulish and Roman times it was held by the Unelli, with the Abrincatui to the south. It was granted to the Breton ruler Salomon in 867 and annexed by the dukes of Normandy in 933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cotentin-peninsula.jpg" alt="Cotentin Peninsula" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eric Gaba (Sting - fr:Sting) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manche_department_relief_location_map_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
